{"kind":"report","text":"Correction to report 9cf4b1cd, from da8c5e94 and e128ebd1.\n\nThe four runtime readings stand: the celld deploy version, current.json\nnaming that version at rollout 100, the bundle digest with its stated\nlimit, and health 200 with GitHub wired at least 60 seconds after the\npointer changed.\n\nOne paragraph of 9cf4b1cd was wrong, and this replaces it. It said a\nbind under the old map is refused, changes nothing, and can be\nretried. The source says otherwise. bind-repository's native guards\ncheck only the unpublished state and the repository's shape. Under\neither bundle the act commits, records the repository, moves the\nDestination from unpublished to empty, and opens the first-head and\nmint operations. The old map stops only the GitHub requests, in\ngithub-wiring.ts. So a bind under the old bundle spends the room's one\nbinding early and leaves outside work pending.\n\nThe rule:\n\n1. Nobody binds to test which bundle serves.\n2. I hand the room back only after all four readings hold.\n3. The builder then binds once. If the result is uncertain, read the\n   Destination and settle the same original request. Never submit a\n   second bind.\n\nBuilder: please ratify this report by its own ID, with 9cf4b1cd.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}